<urn:usf:rule:completion-check-receipts-execution-intent:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before any new canonical check effect, while holding the existing candidate lock, authenticate the current candidate, validation and execution authority. Derive exact execution input and intent identities from those values, not caller data. Create a contained owner-only no-follow PREPARED intent atomically and fsync its file and parent directory; atomically persist and fsync STARTED before child spawn. Refuse unsafe or conflicting pending intent publication without deleting bytes. A read-only receipt-publication snapshot may authenticate only absent receipt paths, one authenticated final receipt with link count one, one authenticated pending receipt with link count one, or authenticated final and pending paths with link count two, identical device, inode, owner, mode and bytes, after rederiving the exact current candidate, basis, validation, runtime-authority dependencies and full receipt claims. Pending-only and final-pending hardlink snapshots are recoverable-not-current: they are never a current receipt, receipt-set member, evidence, completion or terminal claim. STARTED with such a fully current authenticated snapshot remains STARTED and reconciliation-required, never UNKNOWN. SETTLED requires an authenticated final singleton. The ordinary strict receipt reader remains final-only and refuses every pending or hardlinked snapshot. Before native receipt-publication mutation, reauthenticate the same snapshot and require exact before and after candidate, basis, validation, runtime-authority, receipt bytes and file identity equality; movement preserves bytes and refuses. Only the existing native receipt-publication recovery may consume that same snapshot to link or unlink, fsync and then require an authenticated final singleton; read-only recovery never mutates. On every native entry, including legacy explicit execution, inspect retained intent before scratch reset or invocation. A current matching final receipt may reconcile STARTED or SETTLED without execution; STARTED without an authenticated receipt becomes UNKNOWN and refuses redispatch. UNKNOWN remains blocked without an independently authenticated outcome readback. PREPARED is pre-effect only. Persist SETTLED only after current matching final receipt readback, with its exact digest. Do not invent historical intents for current retained receipts. Legacy explicit behavior is unchanged when no intent exists. Required schema fields and state enumeration must agree exactly with current semantic requiredField and allowedState declarations before interpretation. Preserve scalar checked-receipt schema, digest domain, native locks and confinement. Intent records are recovery state, never semantic completion or telemetry authority." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
