<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Only the existing strictNodeTestPaths parser classifies unsupported commands. Preserve its eight-test-path maximum and every grammar/path guard. After read-only currentness and retained receipt/intent handling but before execution-view creation, scratch reset, PREPARED/STARTED persistence or spawn, return CHECK_COMMAND_UNSUPPORTED with closed launchDiagnostic on parser refusal. For test-path-count-exceeded return kind strict-node-test-paths, observedTestPaths and maximumTestPaths 8. Other failures expose only an explicitly compiled native classification, never guessed host causes or raw command tokens. A pre-effect refusal writes no diagnostic or intent and observes no child." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "On actual failed-child observation only, capture stdout and stderr as opaque bytes under the existing combined 262144-byte output limit; retain exact separate observed counters and canonical base64. A signal, timeout or synthesized existing exit result is not an independently observed OS exit status. outputTruncated is true on output-limit termination; false does not certify complete streams. Do not change process settlement, group signals, wall/grace policy, confinement or any existing limit." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Under the existing candidate lock, derive diagnosticPath .usf/diagnostics/check/<candidate-hex>/<validation-path-hash>/<intent-hex>.json using the authenticated candidate and intent digests and existing canonicalDigest(validationObligationIri) path hash. No caller path, identity, command or budget override. All listed requiredField values form a closed private record. diagnosticDigest is canonicalDigest of the exact validated record excluding only diagnosticDigest; base64 is opaque, not recursively interpreted as a filesystem path. Validate actual path fields separately. No signing, independent stream attestation, receipt or acceptance authority is established." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before persistence and every reference readback, rederive the entire current intent binding including candidate tree/workspace facts, exact work/profile/basis/scope, validation command/environment/mode/tool/schema/runtime-authority path and byte denominator and executionInputDigest. Require exact equality to the retained intent. The abbreviated diagnostic fields do not replace full intent authentication. Persist owner-UID mode0600 nlink1 regular file beneath owner-private no-follow ancestry, with bounded reads, atomic publication and file/directory fsync. Preserve conflicting, pending, unsafe, stale or malformed bytes and refuse; never overwrite a different record or treat pending as absence." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Serialized diagnostic bytes are bounded by 4*ceil(262144/3)+65536 = 415064, solely base64 expansion and fixed closed metadata overhead, not extra captured output. Each base64 field has at most349528 characters; native decode/reencode equality and combined decoded length at most262144 are mandatory. Observed counters must be exactly representable nonnegative safe integers, captured lengths cannot exceed observed lengths, and all fields must agree with the actual bounded observation. Reject overflow/noncanonical data, do not fabricate counters." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Authenticate unchanged current binding, persist and read back a failed-child diagnostic, then retain UNKNOWN using the existing intent rule. Crash before persistence invents no diagnostic; crash after persistence before UNKNOWN may return the authenticated pointer while preserving UNKNOWN/no-redispatch semantics. STARTED with a recoverable pending successful receipt retains the existing receipt recovery precedence. Only an authenticated matching final successful receipt may reconcile to SETTLED. Diagnostic metadata never settles an intent, creates a receipt or authorizes retry. Old UNKNOWN records without a log remain UNKNOWN without retrofit." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "On UNKNOWN or unresolved STARTED, return the existing unknown-outcome refusal with a matching diagnostic reference if available, not historical CHECK_FAILED as a fresh execution claim. Unsafe, malformed, oversized, noncanonical, wrong-binding or conflicting diagnostics preserve all state and return CHECK_DIAGNOSTIC_INVALID. A current successful receipt follows existing success/replay semantics and produces no failure diagnostic. No destructive cleanup or fresh child is permitted to repair diagnostic uncertainty." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "GraphDerivedCheckResult and urn:usf:check-result:1 expose only closed optional launchDiagnostic or failureDiagnostic on refusal; ordinary output contains no streams. The shared complete receipt-set consumer retains exact failed obligation, native reason and diagnostic reference, stops later checks and returns no partial set. schemas/check-result.schema.json defines diagnostic extension fragments only; existing basis, receipt and native result validation remains required, not replaced by its intentionally partial envelope." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
<urn:usf:rule:check-failure-diagnostics:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Raw child bytes are sensitive and are not certified sanitized, credential-free or safe for publication. No additional credential, environment, source or host-data collection is permitted. No job/phase/observation identity is inferred. No writes to metrics inputs, .usf/metrics/job-lifecycle-v2.jsonl or Hermes feedback inputs. Existing urn:usf:job-lifecycle-metric-event:2 and urn:usf:hermes-feedback-event:1 semantics are unchanged; this private diagnostic is neither telemetry nor evidence/proof/completion." <urn:usf:graph:check-execution-intent> .
